  "sections": [
    {
      "section_id": "tourniquet_section_1",
      "section_title": "Tourniquet",
      "section_order": 1,
      "subsections": [
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_1",
          "subsection_title": "Introduction",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_1",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/tourniquet_01.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/tourniquet_02.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/tourniquet_03.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A tourniquet is a device used to compress blood vessels and reduce or temporarily stop blood flow to a limb."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "In clinical practice, tourniquets are used principally for two purposes:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Surgical tourniquet: produces a relatively bloodless operative field during selected limb operations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Emergency haemorrhage-control tourniquet: controls life-threatening bleeding from an extremity, especially when direct pressure is ineffective or impractical."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "These two types have different designs, indications, application methods and safety considerations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "OSCE identification statement:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "“This is a tourniquet, a device used to compress blood vessels to control bleeding or temporarily reduce limb perfusion. Surgical pneumatic tourniquets are used to provide a bloodless field during selected extremity operations, while purpose-designed emergency tourniquets are used to control life-threatening limb haemorrhage.”"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_2",
          "subsection_title": "Classification",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_2",
              "group_title": "A. According to purpose",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/tourniquet_04.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "1. Surgical pneumatic tourniquet"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Uses an inflatable cuff connected to a pressure-control unit."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Commonly used in selected orthopaedic and limb procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Allows controlled pressure monitoring."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Requires appropriate cuff selection and trained operation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/tourniquet_05.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "2. Emergency mechanical tourniquet"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Uses a tightening mechanism, often a windlass, to compress the limb."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Used for life-threatening extremity bleeding."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Designed for rapid application and secure locking."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Must be a purpose-designed haemorrhage-control device."
                },
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/tourniquet_06.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "3. Elastic exsanguination bandage / Esmarch-type device"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "An elastic bandage may be used in selected surgical settings to displace blood from a limb before a surgical tourniquet is inflated."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Used only in appropriate circumstances by trained clinicians."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It is not interchangeable with a purpose-designed emergency tourniquet."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It may be inappropriate when infection, tumour or thromboembolic concerns make limb exsanguination unsafe."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_3",
              "group_title": "B. According to mechanism",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Pneumatic inflatable cuff."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Mechanical windlass or ratchet device."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Elastic bandage-based device used for selected surgical purposes."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_3",
          "subsection_title": "Labelled components",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_4",
              "group_title": "A. Pneumatic surgical tourniquet",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "image",
                  "assetPath": "assets/resources/content/surgical/tourniquet_07.webp",
                  "caption": null
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "meddeygo.com",
                    "1. Cuff"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Wraps around the limb. Cuff width and shape must be appropriate for the limb and device."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "2. Inflation tubing"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Connects the cuff to the pressure-control unit."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "3. Pressure display"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Shows the pressure delivered to the cuff."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "4. Pressure control and inflation system"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Allows the operator to set and regulate the cuff pressure according to the clinical protocol."
                },
                {
                  "type": "checklist",
                  "items": [
                    "5. Timer or elapsed-time display"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Helps monitor tourniquet duration."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_5",
              "group_title": "B. Mechanical emergency tourniquet",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Its components may include:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Strap: encircles the limb."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Windlass or tightening mechanism: increases circumferential compression."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Windlass clip or locking mechanism: maintains tension."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Securing strap: prevents loosening."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Application instructions or marker: assists correct use."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The precise components vary by model."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_4",
          "subsection_title": "Principles of operation",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_6",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A tourniquet compresses blood vessels against surrounding tissues."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "In surgical use, sufficient cuff pressure is applied to occlude arterial inflow and venous outflow in the intended region, reducing bleeding within the operative field."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "In emergency use, a purpose-designed tourniquet compresses the limb sufficiently to control life-threatening haemorrhage."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Important distinction: A venous obstruction alone can worsen congestion and bleeding. The aim in surgical use is appropriate vascular occlusion, not merely venous compression."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_5",
          "subsection_title": "Indications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_7",
              "group_title": "A. Surgical tourniquet",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Selected hand and wrist operations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Selected forearm and elbow operations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Selected foot and ankle procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Selected knee and lower-limb operations."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Selected fracture fixation and soft-tissue procedures where a bloodless field improves visualisation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "The suitability of tourniquet use depends on the procedure, the limb, the patient's vascular status and the surgeon's judgement."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_8",
              "group_title": "B. Emergency tourniquet",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Life-threatening extremity haemorrhage."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Severe traumatic bleeding not controlled promptly by direct pressure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Situations where maintaining pressure on a wound is impractical or unsafe."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Selected mass-casualty or prehospital emergencies involving major limb bleeding."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "In life-threatening external bleeding, do not delay haemorrhage control while searching for equipment that is not immediately available."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_6",
          "subsection_title": "Contraindications and precautions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_9",
              "group_title": "Surgical tourniquet",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Potential contraindications or important precautions include:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Significant peripheral arterial disease or compromised limb circulation."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Suspected deep-vein thrombosis or substantial thromboembolic risk."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Severe local infection, depending on the procedure and device."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Sickle cell disease or other conditions where ischaemia may be particularly hazardous; individual assessment is required."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Significant skin injury, burns or fragile tissue at the cuff site."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A limb with vascular reconstruction or a fistula that may be damaged by compression."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Procedures involving infection or tumour where exsanguination may risk spreading infected or tumour-containing material."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "These are not all absolute contraindications in every setting. The decision should be individualised."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_10",
              "group_title": "Emergency tourniquet",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Life-threatening haemorrhage may justify tourniquet use despite other medical concerns. The immediate priority is haemorrhage control."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A purpose-designed limb tourniquet is not appropriate for bleeding from the neck, chest, abdomen or groin where the device cannot safely compress the bleeding source."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_7",
          "subsection_title": "Basic application principles",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_11",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Educational overview only. Follow device-specific instructions and local protocols; surgical tourniquet use requires trained clinical personnel."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_12",
              "group_title": "A. Surgical pneumatic tourniquet",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Assess the limb and document baseline neurovascular status."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Select an appropriately sized cuff for the limb and procedure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Inspect the skin and protect it with the specified interface material."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Apply the cuff in the correct position, ensuring it is secure and free from folds."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Connect the cuff to the pressure-control unit and check the system."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Establish the pressure using an appropriate, procedure-specific protocol, accounting for limb occlusion pressure and the patient's circumstances."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Record the inflation time and monitor the duration continuously."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Monitor the limb, cuff, pressure system and patient throughout the procedure."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Deflate according to the operative plan and monitor for bleeding, haemodynamic changes and reperfusion effects."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Document the deflation time and reassess the limb."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "There is no single universally safe cuff pressure or duration for every patient or operation. The minimum effective pressure and the shortest practical duration should be used according to the relevant protocol."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_13",
              "group_title": "B. Emergency mechanical tourniquet",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Recognise life-threatening limb bleeding and activate emergency assistance."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Apply a purpose-designed tourniquet according to its instructions, generally proximal to the wound and not over a joint."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Tighten it until the bleeding stops; secure the device."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "If bleeding continues, reassess the application and follow the device's instructions for additional haemorrhage control, including a second tourniquet when indicated."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Record the application time."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Arrange urgent transport and definitive medical care."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Do not periodically loosen an emergency tourniquet. Removal or conversion to another haemorrhage-control method should be undertaken by appropriately trained personnel under an appropriate protocol."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_8",
          "subsection_title": "Advantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_14",
              "group_title": "Surgical tourniquet",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Improves visualisation of the operative field."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "May reduce intraoperative blood loss."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can facilitate precise dissection and selected procedures."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Allows controlled, monitored cuff inflation with a pneumatic system."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_15",
              "group_title": "Emergency tourniquet",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can rapidly control life-threatening extremity bleeding."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Frees the rescuer's hands after secure application."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can be applied in prehospital or remote settings."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "May be lifesaving when direct pressure is insufficient."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_9",
          "subsection_title": "Disadvantages",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_16",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Causes temporary tissue ischaemia."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Can injure nerves and soft tissues."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Requires careful attention to duration and pressure in surgical use."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "May cause pain, particularly in an awake patient."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Emergency application may cause discomfort and requires prompt definitive care."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Incorrect application may fail to control bleeding or worsen venous congestion."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A surgical tourniquet may obscure ongoing bleeding in the distal operative field until deflation."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_10",
          "subsection_title": "Complications",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_17",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "table",
                  "columns": [
                    "Complication",
                    "Explanation"
                  ],
                  "rows": [
                    [
                      "Nerve injury",
                      "Compression or ischaemia may cause temporary or permanent neuropathy."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Skin injury",
                      "Pressure, shear or poor cuff positioning may damage skin."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Muscle injury",
                      "Prolonged compression and ischaemia may injure muscle."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Ischaemic injury",
                      "Tissue damage risk increases with inappropriate pressure or duration."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Reperfusion effects",
                      "Deflation can produce metabolic and haemodynamic changes."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Increased postoperative pain",
                      "May occur following surgical tourniquet use."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Venous congestion",
                      "Inadequate occlusion can obstruct venous return without adequately stopping arterial inflow."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Thromboembolic complications",
                      "Risk depends on the patient, procedure and other factors."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Bleeding after deflation",
                      "Previously obscured bleeding may become apparent."
                    ],
                    [
                      "Tourniquet failure",
                      "Poor positioning, incorrect tightening or equipment failure may permit ongoing bleeding."
                    ]
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_18",
              "group_title": "Important emergency point",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "In a patient with traumatic haemorrhage, uncontrolled bleeding is immediately life-threatening. The risks of a correctly applied emergency tourniquet must be weighed against the risk of death from haemorrhage."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_11",
          "subsection_title": "Monitoring and documentation",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_19",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "For surgical tourniquets, record:"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Indication and limb."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Cuff position and size."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Applied pressure and the basis for pressure selection, where required by protocol."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Inflation time."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Deflation time and total duration."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Relevant neurovascular findings."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Any complications or equipment concerns."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "For emergency tourniquets, record the time of application, the location, whether bleeding stopped, and any subsequent changes or interventions."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_12",
          "subsection_title": "High-yield OSCE viva questions",
          "subsection_icon": null,
          "content_groups": [
            {
              "group_id": "tourniquet_group_20",
              "group_title": "",
              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q1. What is a tourniquet?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "A device that compresses blood vessels to control limb bleeding or temporarily reduce limb perfusion."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q2. What are the two major clinical uses?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Creating a bloodless field during selected surgery and controlling life-threatening extremity haemorrhage."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q3. What is the advantage of a pneumatic surgical tourniquet?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "It permits controlled cuff inflation and pressure monitoring."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q4. Name four complications."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Nerve injury, skin damage, muscle ischaemia and reperfusion effects."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q5. Why is tourniquet duration important?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Prolonged compression and ischaemia increase the risk of nerve, muscle and other tissue injury."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q6. Is there one safe pressure and duration for all surgical patients?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "No. Pressure and duration must be selected and monitored according to the patient, limb, procedure and local protocol."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q7. Should an emergency tourniquet be periodically loosened?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "No. Do not periodically loosen it. Maintain haemorrhage control and arrange urgent definitive care."
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Q8. What is the first priority in life-threatening traumatic limb bleeding?"
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "Rapid haemorrhage control and activation of emergency care."
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "subsection_id": "tourniquet_subsection_13",
          "subsection_title": "High-yield comparison",
