              "group_subtitle": null,
              "group_icon": null,
              "blocks": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "text": "“This is a tourniquet, a device used to compress blood vessels and control bleeding or temporarily reduce limb perfusion. Surgical pneumatic tourniquets are used to create a bloodless field during selected limb operations, while purpose-designed emergency tourniquets control life-threatening extremity haemorrhage. Its advantages include improved operative visualisation or rapid haemorrhage control, depending on the type. Complications include nerve injury, skin damage, muscle ischaemia and reperfusion effects. Correct device selection, application, monitoring and documentation are essential.”"
                }
